  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Counter by pushing up",
  "description": "Split the rink into three zones with cones along the boards: each team has its own zone nearest its goal, and between them lies a narrow middle zone around the halfway line. Each team has a goalkeeper and four players in its own zone and a forward in the middle zone. Two players from the other team attack in your zone, so it is 2v4 plus the goalkeeper there.\n\nThe team with more players must win the ball and counter through its forward – with a firm pass along the ice or a lofted ball over the attackers. The forward and one player who skates with them go into the opponents' zone, where they are now outnumbered, and the drill turns the other way. The two who lost the ball skate straight back to help win it back; one of them stays in the middle zone as the new forward. If the goalkeeper catches the ball, they throw it out quickly to their forward. If the ball goes over the end line or the boards, the goalkeeper in that zone restarts with a new ball. Offside applies.\n\nStart more simply without opposition: the team makes three passes in its own zone, plays up to the forward and four players skate up into the other zone. The diagram shows fewer players and is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The first pass after winning the ball goes forward to the forward if they are free – a lofted ball over the attackers is often best."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Forward: get free before the ball is won, and stay onside."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The player who joins in sets off at full speed at once, without waiting to see how it goes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you lose the ball: skate back the shortest way and help the team win it back."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
